{title: It Came Upon a Midnight Clear}
{key: C}
{time: 6/8}

{start_of_verse: 1}
It [C]came u[F]pon a [C]midnight [**]clear that [F]glorious [D]song of [G]old[**]
From [C]angels [F]bending [C]near the [**]earth to [F]touch their [G]harps of [C]gold[**]
Peace [E7]on the [**]earth, good [Am]will to [**]men from [G]heaven's all [D]gracious [G]King[**]
The [C]world in [F]solemn [C]stillness [**]lay, to [F]hear the [G]angels [C]sing[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Still [C]through the [F]cloven [C]skies they [**]come with [F]peaceful [D]wings un[G]furled[**]
And [C]still their [F]heavenly [C]music [**]floats o'er [F]all the [G]weary [C]world[**]
A[E7]bove its [**]sad and [Am]lowly [**]plains, they [G]bend on [D]hovering [G]wing[**]
And [C]ever [F]o'er its [C]Babel [**]sounds the [F]blessed [G]angels [C]sing[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [C]ye, be[F]neath life's [C]crushing [**]load whose [F]forms are [D]bending [G]low[**]
Who [C]toil a[F]long the [C]climbing [**]way with [F]painful [G]steps and [C]slow[**]
Look [E7]now! for [**]glad and [Am]golden [**]hours come [G]swiftly [D]on the [G]wing[**]
O [C]rest be[F]side the [C]weary [**]road and [F]hear the [G]angels [C]sing[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
For [C]lo! The [F]days are [C]hastening [**]on by [F]prophets [D]seen of [G]old[**]
When [C]with the [F]ever [C]circling [**]years shall [F]come the [G]time fore[C]told[**]
When [E7]peace shall [**]cover [Am]all the [**]earth its [G]ancient [D]splendors [G]fling[**]
And [C]the whole [F]world send [C]back the [**]song which [F]now the [G]angels [C]sing[**]!
{end_of_verse}
